// Crown — Martin Lubich's model of the Austrian Imperial Crown
// (loramel.net), distributed in pbrt-v4-scenes, which credits him in its
// README; no separate license text ships with the scene, so permissions
// are per that repo. Gold filigree, pearls, enamel plates, and gems on a
// red velvet cushion under 5500K blackbody area panels — the corpus's
// conductor-Fresnel and dielectric-gem stress test, shot with a wide
// aperture (DOF carries through the import).
//
// Fetch:     scenes/corpus/fetch.sh crown   (pbrt-v4-scenes @ 30cf4a0)
// Bootstrap: cenote-cli import sources/pbrt-v4-scenes/crown/crown.pbrt
//            (re-imports go to scratch for diffing — this file is curated
//            by hand and is the source of truth)
// Oracle:    pbrt-v4 volpath maxdepth 100, halton (native header; compared
//            at 2048 spp). Native film is iso 150 on a canon_eos_5d_mkiv
//            sensor (both unsupported), so the honest comparison rides a
//            film-stripped reference — zero-day's film-response class.
//
// Import fidelity (28 warnings at bootstrap):
// - Eighth-res RMSE vs film-stripped pbrt: 0.304 raw / 0.093
//   display-clamped (cenote 2048 spp; pbrt's 512-vs-2048 self-distance is
//   0.003, so the reference is converged). Against the native film the
//   clamped number is 0.133 — the difference is tone, not shading. Raw is
//   spike-dominated (maxdepth-100 gem caustics); clamped is the signal.
// - Displacement is the dominant divergence: with the four displacement
//   textures removed from pbrt (sapphire bump, the mitra bands), the
//   score collapses to 0.072 raw / 0.048 clamped. pbrt's sapphire is
//   dark and faceted, cenote's smooth clear glass. Unlock = displacement.
// - The ruby/sapphire absorption media are curated onto their materials
//   as Beer-Lambert transmission tint — exact, not approximate (sigma_s
//   is 0), and every binding of those materials carries the medium.
// - Dispersive gem etas (diamond, small_ruby) import as the 1.5 fallback;
//   curated to the visible-range mean 3.4. Unlock = spectral IOR.
// - Two `mix` materials (enamel-on-gold masks) import as OpenPBR
//   defaults; curated to textured metalness — the mask drives
//   metal-vs-diffuse per texel, one constant carries the mask-mean color
//   blend. The curations together are worth 1.5x against the degraded
//   reference (0.071 -> 0.048 clamped). Unlock = mix material.
// - Small documented drops: pbrt's roughness remap cannot ride a texture
//   (texels read as OpenPBR roughness directly, x2); scale factors on
//   textures feeding reflectance/roughness are dropped (0.62, 1.5, 0.1);
//   one equal-axis anisotropic roughness averages exactly.
